summary:
WP-37 is built: stage G of the configuration pipeline, in two new packages. internal/config/convert is the conversion registry. It has a Converter interface that works on generic tree.Node envelopes, including partial overlay documents with $patch and ${VAR}, and an identity converter for ruralz/v1alpha1. The registry reports RZ-CFG-007 for an unserved apiVersion, strips the ruralz.io/conversion-data annotation from the hub form, and holds the RZ-CFG-025 deprecation table from 02 req 76 (empty in M1). internal/config/defaults is stage G itself, and its four steps run in this order:
- Materialize writes every schema default (table-free, read from schemaidx) and the registry defaults slot, failureMode and filterClass (for every type, per R-7) into present objects only. Materialized nodes get StyleDefaulted and the parent's position.
- convert.ToHub converts the tree to the hub form.
- Normalize rewrites Duration, ByteSize and Decimal values, writes integral numbers at integer positions as integer text, and lower-cases host names. It sorts set and map lists and object members in RFC 8785 order. Duplicates that only appear after normalization are RZ-CFG-005, and so is any number the canonical form would not keep (R-64 range rule, skipped for RoleCanonical files). The JSONSchemaDocument value is treated as opaque data (CR 144).
- Decode fills the v1alpha1 kind structs and the registry config types. A decode failure is located by a reflect walk, so the RZ-CFG-005 diagnostic sits at the exact field with a message that is the same with or without GOEXPERIMENT=jsonv2.

Stage.Resource and Stage.Run (a bounded worker pool, all goroutines joined, ctx checked between resources) build the hub.Resource values and the hub.Bundle. Tests cover:
- every schema default, plus a check that the schema defaults equal the +ruralz:default markers in pkg/config/v1alpha1;
- registry defaults for all 23 Policy types;
- the scalar, number, host and list tables;
- a golden of the example Bundle;
- determinism across 1, 2 and 8 workers, idempotence on stage G's own output (R-47), and reorder invariance;
- a round trip of every schema field through each registered converter;
- linear scaling up to 12,000 members per object or list;
- fuzz targets FuzzStageIdempotent, FuzzIntegerText and FuzzConversionRoundTrip, plus benchmarks.
